* GITRUN - run an OS command and see BOTH streams.  See BP/GITSTATUS.
*
* jBASE's own EXECUTE ... CAPTURING takes stdout alone and gives no exit status,
* so a command that failed on stderr -- a licence refusal above all -- reached
* BASIC as silence (mv_git#192).
*
* The status is the DEFC's return value, following every other shim here.  It
* cannot be a third VAR: storing an integer into a VAR the caller passed takes
* the process down with exit 201 and prints nothing.
      SUBROUTINE GITRUN(CMD, ANS, ST)
      DEFC VAR JBGITRUN(VAR, VAR)
      ANS = ""
      ST = JBGITRUN(CMD, ANS)
      RETURN
